            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# wef-notch 0.5.0

**A Theme of your own.** Settings' Theme card has a seventh swatch, **Custom**,
in a new third row beside two fields, **Body** and **Card**. Type or paste a
colour as hex — `#22324A`, `22324a`, either works — and the Panel switches to
it as the last digit lands. Everything else follows from your two colours: the
words turn light or dark by whichever reads better against both. A half-typed
colour changes nothing, and Escape or a click outside ends editing.

Custom starts in navy, a look none of the other six has. Your colours stay
while you wear another Theme, so switching back brings them back.

**Installing for the first time?** Drag `wef-notch.app` into Applications with
the Finder before you open it. Opened from Downloads first, macOS runs it from
a hidden copy: it can't launch at login or update. The README's *Build and
install* says how to put that right.
]]></description>
