            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# wef-notch 0.4.0

**The rest of the week on the Today tab.** Once today's meetings are over,
the tab's meetings half shows what's left of the week — tomorrow through the
last day of your week, as your Mac counts it — each row with its day before
the time (`Thu 10:00`, `Fri All day`). Up to six rows, then `+N more`; a click
opens Calendar. Home, the bar and the meeting alerts still show today only.

On the week's last evening, `Nothing left today` sits in whichever half has
nothing left.

**Installing for the first time?** Drag `wef-notch.app` into Applications with
the Finder before you open it. Opened from Downloads first, macOS runs it from
a hidden copy: it can't launch at login or update. The README's *Build and
install* says how to put that right.

]]></description>
